# Diagnostic Character & Non-Substitution Statement
claim:diagnostic-haired-rhinarium a rdf:Statement ;
    rdf:subject qualia:macropus_giganteus ;
    rdf:predicate q42:diagnosticTrait ;
    rdf:object "finely_haired_rhinarium_with_narrow_bare_black_nostril_rim" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom src:australian-museum-eastern-grey , src:afd-macropus-giganteus ;
    rdfs:comment "Finely haired skin between the nostrils leaving only a narrow bare black rim around each nostril separates Macropus giganteus from Osphranter rufus (bare black rhinarium) and Macropus fuliginosus (darker brown-grey pelage, more extensively dark muzzle)."@en .

